BO_ 1539 CANCTR_SvecConfigCmd: 8 CAN_Master
 SG_ Config_Command : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [1|20] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Config_Value : 8|32@1+ (1,0) [0|4294967295] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Config_Key : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [165|165] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Config_Reserved : 48|8@1+ (1,0) [0|0] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Config_Checksum : 56|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" STM32G474_HRR
CM_ SG_ 1539 Config_Value "Raw u32 transport. Interpret commands 3, 10, and 11..19 as signed two's-complement int32; command 10 is 0.01 degree/bit and commands 11..19 use Q20 scaling.";
CM_ BO_ 1539 "One-shot HRR configuration. Commands 1..3 preserve the legacy persistent SVEC settings. Command 4 starts a safe calibration session with a nonzero u32 token; command 5 finishes using that same token; command 6 aborts using that token or value zero for forced recovery; command 7 selects legacy (0) or calibrated (1) angles. Command 10 supplies a non-persistent manual signed steering reference in 0.01 degrees. Commands 11..18 stage signed row-major IN then OU 2x2 matrix coefficients in Q20; command 19 stages signed phase-per-steer Q20; command 20 packs sample_count in bits0..15, RMS error tenths in bits16..23, and max error tenths in bits24..31. Config_Key must be 0xA5, Config_Reserved zero, and checksum CRC-8/poly-0x07 over ID low, ID high, bytes0..6.";

BO_ 352 CANCTR_TorqueCmd: 7 CAN_Master
 SG_ Torque_Demand : 0|12@1- (1,0) [-2048|2047] "Ncm" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Torque_Demand_Complement : 16|12@1+ (1,0) [0|4095] "raw12" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ REL_Cmd : 32|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ RELE_Cmd : 33|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ OP_Steer_Delta_Up_Limited : 34|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ OP_Steer_Delta_Down_Limited : 35|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ OP_Steer_Max_Limited : 36|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ OP_OutTq_Limited : 37|1@1+ (1,0) [0|1] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Torque_Counter : 40|4@1+ (1,0) [0|15] "" STM32G474_HRR
 SG_ Torque_Checksum : 48|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" STM32G474_HRR
CM_ BO_ 352 "Desired EPS output torque command. Assigned to 0x160 because it was absent from the supplied LS600h Radar bus capture. Torque_Demand uses the low 12 bits of bytes0..1 as a signed Ncm demand, Torque_Demand_Complement is the 12-bit ones-complement in bytes2..3, byte4 carries relay commands plus host limiter bits, Torque_Counter is byte5 bits0..3, and Torque_Checksum is CRC-8 over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 with polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00. In this HRR firmware CANCTR maps +1000 Ncm to -10.0 degrees and -1000 Ncm to +10.0 degrees of SVEC DELTA, clipping outside +-1000 Ncm. Missing or stale commands activate the 250 ms torque interlock, reset SVEC delta, and open REL/RELE.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Torque_Demand "Signed desired EPS output torque demand in Ncm. HRR CANCTR applies inverse-sign scaling: +1000 Ncm produces -10.0 degrees of SVEC DELTA.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Torque_Demand_Complement "12-bit ones-complement redundancy for Torque_Demand, encoded as Torque_Demand raw12 XOR 0x0FFF.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Torque_Counter "4-bit rolling counter carried in byte5 bits0..3.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Torque_Checksum "8-bit CRC over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";

